{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And he shall wring [its neck].</b> With the priest's own [fingers], because it is at the head of the altar, but not with a knife, as it is written: ״כי חרבך הנפת עליה ותחללה״ (for you drew your sword upon it and defiled it). And just as the מליקה spoken of below is from the back of the neck, so too here it is from the back of the neck." "<b>Its head and he shall burn [it].</b> Just as we find burning [done] with the head by itself and the body by itself, so too מליקה — the head by itself and the body by itself, by way of cutting the two signs, in order to fulfill the commandment of separation." "<b>And its blood shall be drained out.</b> All of its blood. How so? The head is held to the body by virtue of not having been cut completely, and it is drained from both of them. And we hold: whatever disqualifies in שחיטה, such as the skin, does not disqualify in הבדלה." "<b>And its blood shall be drained out on the wall of the altar.</b> Because its blood is scant, if he were to receive it in a bowl he would not be able to take from it to sprinkle; therefore he wrings [its neck] at the head of the altar, so that it drains immediately onto the altar."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:41.013312817Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}